{number: 31}
{title: At The Cross}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Alas! And did my Savior bleed?
And [F] did my Sovereign [C] die?
Would He devote that sacred head
For [G7] sinners such as [C] I?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
At the [C] cross, at the cross
Where I [G7] first saw the light,
And the burden of my heart rolled a-[C] way,
It was [F] there by faith I re-[C] ceived my sight,
And now I am [G7] happy all the [C] day!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Was [C] it for crimes that I have done
He [F] groaned upon the [C] tree?
Amazing pity! Grace unknown!
And [G7] love beyond de-[C] gree!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Well [C] might the sun in darkness hide,
And [F] shut his glories [C] in,
When Christ, the mighty Maker, died
For [G7] man the creature's [C] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
But [C] drops of grief can ne’er repay
The [F] debt of love I [C] owe:
Here, Lord, I give my self away,
’Tis [G7] all that I can [C] do!
{end_of_verse}
